I_kwDOQoe6nc8AAAABVBnUYw.body:
If a helper server's shutdown rejects, the VPS fixture disposal loop skips the remaining servers and temporary-root cleanup. Ensure cleanup settles every helper and always attempts the root cleanup, while preserving useful failure information.

Severity: P3 (minor test-infrastructure robustness); CodeRabbit classified this as Minor. The source's sequential awaits and later `releaseFixture()` substantiate the conditional failure path; a rejecting shutdown was not injected during Stage 1 validation. This is deferred follow-up, not a deployment failure or a claim that the fix is complete.

Acceptance:
- An injected helper-shutdown failure still attempts every helper shutdown and temporary-root cleanup.
- The fixture reports cleanup failures without hiding the primary test failure.
- Existing VPS deployment guard cases remain unchanged and pass.

Files: `tests/vps-deploy-guards.test.ts:348`.

Review provenance: PR #907; reviewer `coderabbitai[bot]`; review ID `5409662848`; finding ID `4180483952`; reviewed head `b93c97866d2754a47403d204c68a003042ee2b56`; reviewed base `48d4ba05a6aaa647b3d26135ac3f8625f7688944`; merged as `88b2c2beecaa259495bedfb572490af1ff3008f0`. This is a CodeRabbit finding, not a Codex review finding. Codex's requested review could not start due to its usage limit.

Original finding: https://github.com/ubiquity/ai.ubq.fi/pull/907#discussion_r4180483952

<details>
<summary>Exact original finding text</summary>

_🩺 Stability & Availability_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Dispose can leak resources if a shutdown throws.**

If `server.shutdown()` rejects, the loop exits early. `releaseFixture()` then never runs, so the temp root is not removed. Remaining servers also stay open. Use `try/finally`, and settle all shutdowns first.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   f.dispose = async () => {
-    closeReservations();
-    for (const server of helperServers.splice(0)) await server.shutdown();
-    await releaseFixture();
+    try {
+      closeReservations();
+      await Promise.allSettled(helperServers.splice(0).map((server) => server.shutdown()));
+    } finally {
+      await releaseFixture();
+    }
   };
```
</details>
